      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0008",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "Override this method when the actions you want to perform in response to a state change should be associated with state being exited, or when those actions depend on which state a state machine will enter as a result of the transition.",
      "normalizedSource": "Override this method when the actions you want to perform in response to a state change should be associated with state being exited, or when those actions depend on which state a state machine will enter as a result of the transition.",
      "sourceHash": "155edbc4c0580381097e8c537279773c20aafa67066e599ee76cb06ef4c8e7e8",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Discussion",
      "contextAfter": "For example, in a state machine that manages animations for a 3D character, with Standing, Running, and Jumping states, entering the Jumping state might apply an animation to the character (with a smooth transition from the character’s current pose), and exiting the Jumping state could remove that animation (again with a smooth transition).",
      "documentTitle": "willExit(to:)",
      "framework": "GameplayKit",
      "ko": "",
